    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 1939-05-18; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Well; blood pressure 122/76, pulse 70; weight 89.2 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Examined with Dr. Nakamura: wasting of the first dorsal interosseous and thenar muscles, left more than right; fasciculations in both arms, thighs and calves; grip and finger abduction 4/5 on the right and 4-/5 on the left; left ankle dorsiflexion 4-/5; reflexes brisk with spread, Hoffmann sign present on both sides, left plantar extensor; jaw jerk normal; tongue normal; sensation normal</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>No accessory muscle use; normal chest expansion</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

